---
description: GreenCarWash stack, service boundaries, and API conventions
alwaysApply: true
---

Stack: ASP.NET Core 8 Web API, EF Core + Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.SqlServer, JWT Bearer, FluentValidation, Serilog, Polly, MailKit, NUnit+Moq+FluentAssertions, Swagger.

Pattern per service: Controller -> Service -> Repository -> DbContext. DTOs only in controllers, never return entities.

Database per service. NO cross-database joins or FKs. Cross-service data only via REST (typed HttpClient + Polly).

All times UTC, stored as DATETIME2. Money decimal(10,2). Enums stored as strings.

Global exception middleware returning ProblemDetails. Serilog with CorrelationId. Correct HTTP codes (200/201/400/401/403/404/409/500).

Internal endpoints protected by role "Service" (service JWT or X-Internal-Key).

No frontend. The washer queue is NOT in the database; it is an in-memory structure in code (WasherService).

Follow docs/schema.sql exactly.
